Role Summary

Maintain production equipment running.

&nbsp;

ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:

• Perform preventive, predictive, and corrective maintenance on facility and production equipment.&nbsp;

• Diagnose mechanical, electrical, pneumatic, and hydraulic equipment failures using standard testing equipment and troubleshooting techniques.&nbsp;

• Repair, replace, align, adjust, and install machinery components and equipment.&nbsp;

• Independently perform maintenance work orders with limited supervision.&nbsp;

• Read and interpret blueprints, schematics, manuals, and technical documents.&nbsp;

• Conduct equipment inspections to identify wear, safety concerns, and operational deficiencies.&nbsp;

• Perform routine welding, fabrication, and machining tasks as needed for repairs.&nbsp;

• Maintain accurate maintenance records, parts usage, and completed work documentation within CMMS or maintenance tracking systems.&nbsp;

• Support equipment startups, shutdowns, and changeovers.

&nbsp;

Safety, Compliance and Responsibilities

• Comply with OSHA, company safety policies, environmental regulations, and maintenance standards.

• Maintain clean and organized work areas.

• Participate in safety meetings and incident investigations as required.

• Respond to emergency breakdowns in a timely manner.

• Prioritize maintenance activities based on operational needs.

• Coordinate with production, operations, contractors, and other maintenance personnel.

• Maintain inventory awareness and communicate parts/material needs.

• Provide guidance and technical assistance to Jr. Mechanic employees as assigned.

• Assist in training lower-level mechanics on maintenance procedures and safety practices.

• Work independently on moderately complex maintenance assignments.

&nbsp;

OTHER FUNCTIONS

This position also performs other projects for the company as needed.

&nbsp;

